🔗 Linked List is a dynamic data structure used to store a collection of elements called nodes.
 
Each node contains data and a link → to the next node in the sequence.
 
Unlike arrays, linked lists do not require continuous memory locations, making insertion ➕ and deletion ➖ easier at suitable positions. 

Linked lists are widely used in stacks, queues, and other data structures.

Understanding linked lists creates a strong foundation for learning advanced DSA concepts → 🚀.